features.what_it_does:
A cloud mock returns the best-matching saved example:
- filters by HTTP method;
- honours x-mock-response-code, -id and -name headers;
- scores URL matches, deducting for trailing slash (−5), case (−10), wildcard (−20), IDs (−21) and document distance (−30);
- applies a query-parameter match percentage and optional body/header matching (x-mock-match-request-body/headers);
- echoes wildcard path variables into responses and can add a fixed delay.
Limits: HTTP-only collections; mocks created from a collection are public unless set private.

pain_points:
Capture limits:
- only one proxy or Interceptor session at a time; the proxy is desktop-only;
- media bodies are not captured;
- Interceptor needs a signed-in internal workspace with edit access, plus Bridge on Linux;
- past breakages: 'Error creating interceptor session' (2022), missing PATCH bodies and responses (2021).
https://learning.postman.com/docs/use/capturing-request-data/interceptor/ ; https://github.com/postmanlabs/postman-app-support/issues/11451 ; https://community.postman.com/t/21385
